{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"2128","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"C. Leftmost Below"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"2 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Consider an array $$$a_1, \\ldots, a_n$$$. Initially, $$$a_i = 0$$$ for every $$$i$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You can do operations of the following form. "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" You choose an integer $$$x$$$ greater than $$$\\min(a)$$$. "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" Then, $$$i$$$ is defined as the minimum index such that $$$a_i \\lt x$$$. In other words, $$$i$$$ is the unique integer between $$$1$$$ and $$$n$$$ inclusive such that $$$a_i \\lt x$$$ and $$$a_j \\geq x$$$ for every $$$1 \\leq j \\leq i-1$$$. "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" Finally, $$$a_i$$$ is incremented by $$$x$$$. "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For example, if $$$a = [6, 8, 2, 1]$$$ and you choose $$$x = 6$$$, then $$$i$$$ will be equal to $$$3$$$ (since $$$a_1 \\geq 6$$$, $$$a_2 \\geq 6$$$, and $$$a_3 \\lt 6$$$) and $$$a$$$ will become $$$[6, 8, 8, 1]$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You can do as many operations as you want. Can you reach a target array $$$b_1, \\ldots, b_n$$$?"}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Each test contains multiple test cases. The first line contains the number of test cases $$$t$$$ ($$$1 \\le t \\le 10\\,000$$$). The description of the test cases follows. "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line of each test case contains a single integer $$$n$$$ ($$$2 \\leq n \\leq 200\\,000$$$)."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The second line of each test case contains $$$n$$$ integers $$$b_1, b_2, \\ldots, b_n$$$ ($$$1 \\le b_i \\le 10^9$$$)."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The sum of $$$n$$$ over all test cases does not exceed $$$200\\,000$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For each test case, print "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"YES"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" if you can reach the target array and "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"NO"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" otherwise."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You can output the answer in any case (upper or lower). For example, the strings \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"yEs"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\", \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"yes"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\", \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Yes"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\", and \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"YES"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" will be recognized as positive responses."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Example"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n4\n4\n5 6 1 1\n3\n3 1 2\n3\n40 60 90\n2\n1 1\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\nYES\nNO\nNO\nYES\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the first test case, we can do the following sequence of operations: "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" we choose $$$x=2$$$, $$$a$$$ becomes $$$[2, 0, 0, 0]$$$ "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" we choose $$$x=2$$$, $$$a$$$ becomes $$$[2, 2, 0, 0]$$$ "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" we choose $$$x=3$$$, $$$a$$$ becomes $$$[5, 2, 0, 0]$$$ "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" we choose $$$x=4$$$, $$$a$$$ becomes $$$[5, 6, 0, 0]$$$ "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" we choose $$$x=1$$$, $$$a$$$ becomes $$$[5, 6, 1, 0]$$$ "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" we choose $$$x=1$$$, $$$a$$$ becomes $$$[5, 6, 1, 1]$$$ "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the second test case, we can prove there is no way to reach $$$[3, 1, 2]$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"C","problemCode":"2128C","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/2128/problem/C"}